"""Durotar needed no new speeches in the story pass; its accept lines are in durotar_beats. Three speeches
now name the place they send you, because the old accept line used to carry it."""

STORY = {
    'durotar_skullrock_approach': ("I'm Bloodwarden Ashgrym. You'll have come up from the valley, so you've met these people already, though you don't know it yet.\n\nThat Burning Blade coven you cut out of the ridge back in the Valley wasn't the cult. It was the part that wandered too far from the nest and got sloppy. Skull Rock is the nest. Searing Blade Scouts and raiders work the Skull Rock Approach, out the gate and east, and they work it properly, with overlapping patrols and relief points. Somebody out there has had training.\n\nClear the approach before anyone goes near the cave mouth. That's an order, not a suggestion, because the cave is worse, and I'd rather you walked into it without half the patrol already shouting. I've fought this cult before. Don't rush it.", None),
    'dur_houndmaster': ("Houndmaster Kraygh keeps his dogs on the approach and his whip in his hand, and in four months of watching I've never once seen him sleep. I climbed that cliff at every hour of the day and night to catch him at it.\n\nThe Burning Blade bring him fresh hounds up out of the caves, and he sets them on any traveller who looks too far in. He doesn't set them on raiders or soldiers. He sets them on travellers, because a traveller doesn't come back with friends. I want him gone before those hounds find their way down to the road.\n\nHe's by the cave mouth on the Skull Rock Approach, east of here. Cut down the Searing Blade Raiders first, because they hold the hounds until he gives the word. And when the whip cracks, don't run away from him. Run past him.", None),
    'dur_matron_sowbelly': ("She was an ordinary sow. I want to start there, because everyone who sees her assumes she came out of the ground that way. She was the farm's breeding stock. I watched her being led in off a cart six years ago, and I couldn't have picked her out of a pen.\n\nThen the quilboar fed her whatever they feed things. Now she's the size of a cart and twice as bitter, and the whole farm has arranged itself round her. The razorbacks follow her, and I've watched the farmhands pray to her in rows at dusk. She isn't livestock any more. She's the reason they stay.\n\nShe's in the barn at the back of the furrows at Rocktusk Farm, south of here. She hits hard and smells worse. Don't fight her in the open, because the razorbacks will join in, and they won't hesitate.", None),
}
